samtools/htscodecs, release v1.6.7 (see version.h).
Upstream: https://github.com/samtools/htscodecs

Only the files karyozip's Makefile compiles, and the headers they reach,
are kept. Deleted from the upstream tree: fqzcomp_qual, rANS_static,
rANS_byte.h, htscodecs.c/.h, permute.h, varint2.h, tokchunk, and the
AVX2, AVX512, NEON and SSE4 rANS variants, which rANS_static32x16pr.c
never references under this config.h.

One local patch: rANS_static4x16pr.c adds "#include <asm/hwcap.h>" in the
aarch64 branch, so HWCAP_* is defined on older glibc. It is dead on x86.
Every other file is byte-identical to upstream, and config.h and
version.h are generated by upstream's build rather than shipped.

Resync by copying the same subset from a new tag and re-applying that one
include; fix everything else in karyozip.c.
